Ok, you are right, the ftp.uu.net code is correct.  I applied my patch,
and it was happy, so I though the error wasn't fixed.  Today, I ftp'd the
entire package from ftp.uu.net, and compared it with what I got from some
other comp.sources.games archive site (don't ask me which, it was a long
time ago).  I came up with two differences, one in MANIFEST, and the other
in "osave.c".  The code in my version looks like:

in save_player()...

  /* Save player item knowledge */
  for (i=0;i<TOTALITEMS;i++)
    fwrite((char *)&(Objects[i].known),sizeof(Objects[i].known),1,fd);
}

in restore_player()...

#ifndef MSDOS
    fread((char *)&(Objects[i].known),sizeof(int),1,fd);
#else
    fread((char *)&(Objects[i].known),sizeof(Objects[i].known),1,fd);
#endif
}

That code won't work for me.

Now, the bigger question is why is there more than one "official" version?
I've supplied a lot of people with the osave.c patch so I suspect there are
a lot of archive sites that have the problem.

